            <ArticleTitle>[Hemolytic anemia caused by excessive use of analgesics].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>52-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 40-year-old female patient is reported who gave a history of analgesics abuse (phenacetin) and had haemolytic anaemia. The probable mechanism of the toxic effect of phenacetin on the haemopoietic system through induction of intravascular haemolysis (so called stibophen-type haemolysis) is discussed. One-year follow-up demonstrated the reversibility of these haematological changes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
